"""Generate concise reviewable report from completed validation tables."""
import json
import numpy as np
import pandas as pd
from round2_train import ROOT

def md(df):
    def f(v):
        if isinstance(v,(float,np.floating)):return f'{v:.5g}' if np.isfinite(v) else '—'
        return str(v)
    return '| '+' | '.join(map(str,df.columns))+' |\n| '+' | '.join(['---']*len(df.columns))+' |\n'+'\n'.join('| '+' | '.join(f(v) for v in row)+' |' for row in df.itertuples(index=False,name=None))

def main():
    res=ROOT/'results';lock=json.loads((ROOT/'configs/locked_tcn.json').read_text());missions=lock['missions']
    allr=pd.read_csv(res/'all_runs.csv');m=pd.read_csv(res/'mission_comparison.csv');seed=pd.read_csv(res/'seed_robustness.csv');fam=pd.read_csv(res/'family_comparison.csv');ch=pd.read_csv(res/'channel_comparison.csv');budget=pd.read_csv(res/'epoch_budget.csv');screen=pd.read_csv(res/'screen_summary.csv')
    locked=m[m.model.isin([x['name'] for x in missions.values()])];mainrows=[]
    for row in locked.itertuples():
        f=m[(m.spacecraft==row.spacecraft)&(m.model=='fixed_GCN_80')].iloc[0]
        mainrows.append(dict(Mission=row.spacecraft,Channels=row.channels,TCN_MSE=row.macro_mse,Fixed_GCN_MSE=f.macro_mse,Macro_reduction_pct=100*(1-row.macro_mse/f.macro_mse),Median_paired_reduction_pct=row.median_pct_gain_vs_fixed80,W_L_T=f'{row.wins}/{row.losses}/{row.ties}'))
    text=['# Round 2: validation-only TCN-GCN confirmation','',
    'For discussion with the research team. This study used only the first 80% of the official TRAIN arrays. The final 20% calibration block and all TEST arrays/anomaly labels remained unexamined in this round. The original study and supplied experiment outputs are preserved. No anomaly precision, recall or F-score was calculated or used for selection.', '',
    '## Recommendation and main result','',
    'Lock the mission-specific TCN configurations below for subsequent calibration and later anomaly evaluation. Keep all three seeds (17, 29, 43) and report their distribution; do not pick a winning seed or describe averages of model metrics as an ensemble. These are forecasting results, not evidence of improved anomaly detection.','',
    md(pd.DataFrame(mainrows)), '',
    'MSE is per-channel fit-standardized one-step telemetry error, averaged equally over channels after averaging the three seeds. W/L/T compares per-channel three-seed mean MSE with matched-budget fixed GCN, with absolute tolerance 1e-7. The paired percentage median uses channels whose original fixed-GCN validation MSE exceeds 1e-4. All channels, including zero-error channels, remain in macro MSE and W/L/T.', '',
    '## Audit and study design','',
    'The supplied tensor orientation, causal left padding, graph aggregation and persistence residual are correct. Seven executable audit checks pass. The key finding is that two kernel-3 layers at dilations 1 and 2 have a receptive field of only seven observations, regardless of nominal lookback. No mandatory architectural correction was needed. A suffix-only convolution optimization preserves the final output and legacy two-layer state names; small floating-point changes can affect training trajectories. The maximum discrepancy between supplied and reproduced first-40-epoch MSE is recorded in `results/uploaded_reproduction_check.csv`.', '',
    'The original fit/validation/calibration division remains 60/20/20, with fit-only scaling, varying-command selection and graph construction. The target is one telemetry series; other nodes represent command context, not independent spacecraft sensors. SMAP uses the fixed command-to-target star and MSL the original fit-selected top-four command support. No learned edges were combined with the TCN. Validation is rolling one-step prediction using observed past values, not an open-loop forecast.', '',
    'Seven configurations per mission were screened on six preselected validation-informed channels per mission: native-width RF7, alternate-width RF7, width-64 RF7, kernel-5 RF13, and width-16 dilated stacks with RF63/RF127/RF255 and lookbacks 64/128/250. The longest stack has theoretical RF255 but can observe at most 250 real window positions. To keep fit targets identical across lookbacks, all candidates start fitting at target index 64; longer windows use standardized-zero padding before the array start. This startup convention is introduced here and matters for short streams.', '',
    'Of 84 planned screening fits, 81 completed. The remaining three SMAP RF255 fits were interrupted once an exact lower bound showed that even maximally favorable missing clipped scores could not beat the fully evaluated alternative. This computation-only pruning was introduced during execution; the selection criterion did not change. The numerical proof is retained in `screen_pruning_note.json`. Screening selected the native incumbent plus at most one alternative per mission using a pre-recorded, floor-stabilized clipped-log MSE ratio. Alternatives needed at least 2% improvement over the incumbent on the screen, then on both the full mission and channels excluded from screening. Eligible candidates were confirmed at seeds 17, 29 and 43; the final choice uses the mean selection score across seeds. Screening channels are listed in `configs/screen_protocol.json`; decision files retain every promotion/rejection. The nonscreen comparison reduces screening overfit but is still validation-based selection, not an independent generalization estimate.', '',
    md(screen[['spacecraft','configuration','ratio_to_incumbent','promoted','completed_runs','pruned']]), '',
    'Fresh original fixed-GCN models use the same 80-epoch ceiling and three seeds. Archived compact LSTM, MLP and learned-edge references retain their original 40-epoch budgets; they are secondary comparisons. No LR or dropout search was justified by the short-context results. Deep-stack failures sometimes involve early plateaus, so this screen does not establish that longer context could never help with a different optimization design.', '',
    '## Locked configuration','']
    cfgrows=[]
    for mission,c in missions.items():cfgrows.append(dict(Mission=mission,Hidden=c['hidden'],Lookback=c['lookback'],Kernel=c['kernel_size'],Dilations=str(c['dilations']),Graph=c['graph'],Epoch_ceiling=c['epochs']))
    text += [md(pd.DataFrame(cfgrows)), '',
    'Shared settings: learning rate 0.001; AdamW; weight decay 0.0001; batch target 256 (balanced minibatch partition); gradient norm clipping 1; patience 6; minimum improvement 1e-7; ReLU; no dropout; zero-initialized residual head plus persistence. Restore the best validation epoch separately for every channel/seed. Do not change graph support, seed policy, threshold policy or model choice based on future test-label metrics. Exact settings and schema are in `configs/locked_tcn.json`. Width changes alter capacity as well as optimization; tuned-model gains are not a pure temporal-encoder attribution.', '',
    '## Robustness, families and error scale','',md(seed), '']
    for mission,d in ch.groupby('spacecraft'):
        i=d[d.informative];f=fam[(fam.spacecraft==mission)&(fam.informative>0)].sort_values('median_pct_gain',ascending=False)
        top=', '.join(f"{r.family} ({r.median_pct_gain:.1f}%)" for r in f.head(3).itertuples());bad=', '.join(f"{r.family} ({r.median_pct_gain:.1f}%)" for r in f[f.median_pct_gain<0].itertuples()) or 'none at the family-median level'
        text += [f"**{mission}:** {len(d)-len(i)}/{len(d)} channels are below the original-MSE informative cutoff. Largest family-median reductions versus fixed GCN: {top}. Negative family-median reductions: {bad}. Prefixes are descriptive channel groups, not verified spacecraft subsystems.", '']
    text += ['`channel_comparison.csv` includes absolute standardized MSE, raw-unit MSE, seed standard deviation/range, persistence, and absolute gains for every channel. Raw-unit errors should not be pooled across different telemetry units. `family_comparison.csv` supplies every family, including small groups where medians are fragile. `mission_comparison.csv` includes exploratory channel-bootstrap intervals for stabilized ratios; these do not correct for repeated selection or dependence among channels.', '',
    '![Three-seed validation MSE comparison](figures/validation_scatter.png)', '',
    '## Baseline comparisons','',md(m[['spacecraft','model','budget','seeds','macro_mse','robust_ratio_vs_fixed80']]), '',
    'Ratio below one favors the row model over the new 80-epoch fixed GCN; it is the exponentiated mean clipped log ratio with floor 1e-4 on the informative channel subset. It is not a ratio of aggregate MSE. The archived compact LSTM is not a reproduction of the published Hundman anomaly detector, and no new comparison with published anomaly F-scores is appropriate at this stage.', '',
    '## Training budget and cost','',md(budget[budget.configuration.isin([c['name'] for c in missions.values()])][['spacecraft','seed','runs','improved_after40','best_epoch80','trained_to80','median_epoch','sum_run_wall_seconds']]), '',
    f"There are {len(allr)} unique newly executed fits after removing reused queue entries. Their summed per-run training/evaluation wall times are {allr.seconds.sum()/60:.1f} minutes; concurrent-worker sums are not elapsed study time or isolated CPU benchmarks. Preprocessing and serialization are excluded from the per-run timer. Parameter ranges, epochs, early stops, ceiling hits and individual times are retained in `computational_cost.csv` and `all_runs.csv`. Long-context screening accounts for substantial extra cost. A worker-session interruption required restarting four unfinished RF255 fits with equivalent suffix computation also optimized for windows shorter than RF; see `runtime_resume.json`. Their timings are not directly comparable with earlier RF255 timings. Reported sums include completed fits only and exclude time spent in interrupted fits; they therefore understate total compute consumed. Hardware/backend and convolution implementation differences prevent fair speed comparisons with the user's earlier laptop timings.", '',
    'The 40-versus-80 comparison is taken from the same uninterrupted optimizer trajectory. Some runs still hit the 80-epoch ceiling, so convergence is not guaranteed. Early stopping can also stop before a deeper model learns a useful residual. No ceiling, learning-rate or seed decision used anomaly labels.', '',
    '## Remaining limits and exact next local experiment','',
    '- One chronological validation interval per channel; repeated validation selection can overfit it. Three seeds assess optimization variability, not temporal or mission generalization.',
    '- Longer receptive fields also change network depth; selected widths change capacity. These are controlled fixed-graph configuration comparisons, not complete causal ablations of each design choice. No new TCN-without-edges ablation was run, so these results alone do not establish the graph contribution.',
    '- Some models remain ceiling-limited; archived LSTM/MLP/learned-edge controls have a smaller budget. Family sample sizes vary and near-zero channels make unfiltered percentages unstable.',
    '- Forecasting MSE improvements need not improve anomaly ranking or calibrated alarms. The earlier study already examined NASA test results; a future assessment must not be called a virgin holdout.', '',
    'Next, execute the supplied **TRAIN-only calibration** command locally after accepting the lock:', '',
    '```bash\npython src/calibrate_locked_later.py --output local_calibration\n```', '',
    'It uses the reserved final 20% of TRAIN with each locked checkpoint, retaining all seeds. It records absolute forecast errors, EWMA span 10 (`adjust=True`), startup burn-in `min(10, n/4 rounded down)`, threshold floor `max(1e-8, fit_scale * 1e-6)`, and the inherited 0.995 calibration quantile. It neither refits models nor accesses TEST or anomaly labels. This script was syntax-checked but deliberately not executed here. Only after calibration is frozen should the later anomaly-label evaluation run under a separately fixed reporting protocol.', '',
    'All new code/configurations, checkpoints, learning curves, predictions, source hashes, plots and reproducible CSVs are included in the Round 2 package. See `README.md` for commands and `Audit.md` for the full technical audit.']
    (ROOT/'Round2_Report.md').write_text('\n'.join(text)+'\n')
    brief=['# TCN-GCN validation confirmation — Round 2', '', 'Recommendation: retain the simple two-layer causal TCN and lock the mission-specific widths below. All choices used TRAIN forecasting validation only. Calibration and NASA test anomaly evaluation have not been performed in this round.', '', md(pd.DataFrame(mainrows)), '', 'MSE is the channel-macro mean of fit-standardized validation error, averaged over seeds 17, 29 and 43. The fixed GCN received the same 80-epoch ceiling. W/L/T counts channel improvements, regressions and ties.', '', '**Configuration to lock:**', '', md(pd.DataFrame(cfgrows)), '', 'Both use kernel 3, dilations 1/2, effective receptive field 7, AdamW learning rate 0.001, weight decay 0.0001, patience 6, minimum improvement 1e-7, minibatch target 256, gradient clipping 1, ReLU, no dropout and a persistence residual. Keep all three seeds; restore the best validation epoch for each model.', '', '**What was tested:** 81 of 84 planned screening fits across seven configurations per mission and six channels; three uncompetitive fits were excluded by an exact score bound. The screen spanned widths 16/32/64 and receptive fields 7/13/63/127/255. Promising alternatives had to improve on channels outside the screen before three-seed confirmation. Graph support, data splits and preprocessing stayed fixed. The uploaded TCN is causal and correctly oriented; its nominal 64-step window only uses the final seven observations. Seven correctness tests pass, including checkpoint/output and gradient equivalence checks.', '']
    for mission in missions:
        z=seed[seed.spacecraft==mission];br=budget[(budget.spacecraft==mission)&(budget.configuration==missions[mission]['name'])];row=locked[locked.spacecraft==mission].iloc[0]
        brief += [f"**{mission} robustness:** stabilized paired MSE ratios versus fixed GCN range from {z.robust_ratio.min():.3f} to {z.robust_ratio.max():.3f} across the three seeds (below 1 favors TCN). {row.informative_channels}/{row.channels} channels exceed the near-zero-error cutoff. {int(br.best_epoch80.sum())}/{int(br.runs.sum())} selected-model runs still have their best epoch at 80.", '']
    brief += ['**Limits:** One chronological validation interval, repeated validation-based selection, small family groups and some ceiling-limited fits. Width changes alter model capacity. Archived LSTM/MLP/learned-edge references retain their smaller 40-epoch budget. Better forecasting does not guarantee better anomaly detection.', '', '**Next local experiment:** run `python src/calibrate_locked_later.py --output local_calibration` from the Round 2 folder. This uses only the reserved final 20% of TRAIN with the frozen models and inherited threshold policy; it does not open NASA TEST or labels. The script is supplied but intentionally unexecuted.', '', 'The full audit, baseline/family/seed tables, costs, exact lock, code, checkpoints and reproduction instructions are retained in the accompanying research package. See `Round2_Report.md`, `Audit.md`, `README.md` and `results/`.']
    (ROOT/'Round2_Summary.md').write_text('\n'.join(brief)+'\n')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
